We are to find the length of GJ, which is the **hypotenuse** (the side opposite the right angle).

### Use the Pythagorean Theorem:
In a right triangle:

> **(Hypotenuse)² = (Leg₁)² + (Leg₂)²**

So,

> GJ² = GH² + HJ²  
> GJ² = 5² + 12²  
