- Hypotenuse = c (unknown)

By the **Pythagorean Theorem**:

> $ c^2 = a^2 + b^2 $

Let’s plug in the values:

> $ c^2 = 4^2 + 14^2 = 16 + 196 = 212 $

So,

> $ c = \sqrt{212} $

Now simplify $ \sqrt{212} $:

> $ 212 = 4 \times 53 $  
> So, $ \sqrt{212} = \sqrt{4 \times 53} = \sqrt{4} \cdot \sqrt{53} = 2\sqrt{53} $

